    "narrative": "For the July 11th slate, the **Austin Waves** offense is headlined by the elite efficiency of **Jackson Merrill** (75.26) and **Gunnar Henderson** (69.90). **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a strong matchup against Yesavage, where his profile is boosted significantly by a +13% adjustment for the opposing starter\u2019s skill set and a favorable slot in the two-hole. **Gunnar Henderson** remains our primary catalyst; despite the efficiency penalty for the opposing starter\u2019s ability to hold runners (33% SB), the +16% park factor adjustment makes him a must-start at the top of the order. **Kyle Tucker** (69.75) rounds out our top-tier plays, providing steady production against Pfaadt, bolstered further by the base strength of his profile and a lack of restrictive platoon penalties.\n\nWe are leveraging significant platoon advantages today, most notably with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (56.38) and **Coby Mayo** (62.95). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** receives a +14% dynamic platoon bump against Schlittler, which helps mitigate the negative impact of facing a pitcher with a sub-3.00 xERA. Meanwhile, **Coby Mayo** is a priority play, as the combination of his platoon edge and a +16% park factor elevates him well above his base projection, effectively nullifying the drag of his position in the seven-hole. On the bench, **Miguel Vargas** (52.17) was the most difficult exclusion. While his 0.398 xwOBA is enticing, the combination of an elite-tier catcher pop time and a pitcher proficient at holding runners (60% SB) lowered his ceiling enough that he could not crack the starting nine over the higher-efficiency profiles of **Josh Jung** or **Andy Pages**.\n\nAs we monitor the board, we must keep a close watch on **Liam Hicks** (55.48), whose status as the lead-off hitter is vital; any fluctuation in his batting order could immediately shift him from a marginal start to a bench candidate. While our current lineup is optimized for maximum efficiency, we must remain cognizant of the risk inherent in starting **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (59.87) against Buehler, as the -7% platoon penalty is a non-trivial drag on his production. No major weather concerns have been flagged, but as always, we are prioritizing the daily efficiency scores to ensure we manage our games-played caps effectively across this high-upside matchup set.",
